# Sitters4Us runtime configuration: TEMPLATE ONLY (committed, no real values).
#
# 1. Copy this file to ".env" in the same folder (the repo root, next to
#    PetSitters.csproj). ".env" is git-ignored: NEVER commit it or share it;
#    it contains the database password and this repository is public.
# 2. Fill in the real value. Build as usual: the build copies .env next to
#    PetSitters.exe (bin\Debug or bin\Release), where the app reads it at launch.
# 3. No .env (or no DATABASE_URL) = the app uses only the local SQLite database.
#
# Real environment variables with the same names override this file.

# Cloud database (MySQL 8). The app tries this first at launch, and falls back
# to the local SQLite database if it can't connect.
# Format: mysql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?ssl-mode=REQUIRED
# %-encode special characters in the password (e.g. @ -> %40, : -> %3A, # -> %23).
# ssl-mode: REQUIRED (default: encrypted), VERIFY_CA / VERIFY_IDENTITY (also check
# the certificate), PREFERRED, DISABLED.
# Uncomment and fill in (left commented, the app simply uses the local database):
# DATABASE_URL=mysql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?ssl-mode=REQUIRED

# Optional. "sqlite" (or "local") = always use the local database, even if DATABASE_URL is set
# (the UI tests run like this). "auto" (default) = cloud first, then local.
# PETSITTERS_DB=auto

# Optional. Seconds to wait for the cloud database at launch before falling
# back (1-60, default 8).
# DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=8
